<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Canary Islands</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Canary Islands are an archipelago of volcanic islands in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-ocean">Atlantic Ocean</a> off the north-west coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>, today an autonomous community of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>. Inhabited by the indigenous Guanches, they were reached by the Genoese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lanzarotto-malocello">Lanzarotto Malocello</a> in the early fourteenth century and conquered by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> between 1402 and 1496. They became a key stopover on Spanish voyages to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/canary-islands.jpg" alt="Canary Islands" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Zirland · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Canary_Islands.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
